## Phase 1 — Reconnaissance

### Nmap Port Scan

```bash
nmap -sC -sV -p- 10.10.X.X
```

**Flags explained:**
- `-sC` — Run default NSE scripts for service fingerprinting
- `-sV` — Detect service and version information
- `-p-` — Scan all 65535 ports to avoid missing services on non-standard ports

**Results:**

| Port | State | Service | Version |
|------|-------|---------|---------|
| 22   | open  | ssh     | OpenSSH 7.6p1 Ubuntu |
| 80   | open  | http    | Apache httpd 2.4.29 (Ubuntu) |

Only two ports are open. The main attack surface is port 80 (HTTP). SSH on port 22 will be useful later once credentials are found.

