## Phase 4 — Remote Code Execution via Theme Editor

With admin credentials, we have full access to the WordPress dashboard. WordPress admins can edit theme PHP files directly from the dashboard — this is our path to remote code execution (RCE).

### Step 1 — Log into WordPress Admin

Navigate to `http://internal.thm/blog/wp-admin` and log in with `admin:my2boys`.

### Step 2 — Inject a PHP Reverse Shell

Go to: **Appearance → Theme Editor → Select: Twenty Seventeen → 404 Template (404.php)**

Replace the contents of `404.php` with a PHP reverse shell. You can get one from `/usr/share/webshells/php/php-reverse-shell.php` on Kali. Update the IP and port in the shell to match your attacker machine.

The file is accessible at:

```
http://internal.thm/blog/wp-content/themes/twentyseventeen/404.php
```

### Step 3 — Set up a Listener and Trigger the Shell

On your attacker machine:

```bash
nc -lvnp 4444
```

Then visit the 404.php URL in your browser to execute the shell. You'll receive a reverse connection as the `www-data` user — the web server service account.

